Yes, but you have to remember a few things.

1) You need to drop your stuff on Elbereth.  If it wasn't engraved at a 
minimum, you might rub it out.  And otherwise, a monster walking into 
the room while you're bathing might grab your stash.

2) You can't drop your stuff until you've dug up the fountain, as I 
suspect pools can form anywhere in the room.

3) If you're careless in dropping your stuff, or try to only drop _part_ 
of your stuff as insurance against critters, you might forget which 
things are metal and which aren't -- I have a rusty wand of lightning 
and a rusty ring of polymorph control at this very moment because of 
that -- not like it really matters, admittedly.

All of these are resources; many of these will trip someone up who 
didn't know of the possibility or was careless.  3) seems to be a 
biggie.  To concede too many things as "busywork" does remove some of 
the challenge.

